From: OCCTSwift ecosystem <noreply@secondmouse.au>
Subject: [PATCH] Modeling Algorithms - BRepFilletAPI_MakeFillet builds fillets that
 share a corner and replaces an open result, in the fallback of patch 0060

Patch 0060 builds fillets whose arcs cross, or that run out of face, as the intersection of the
shape filleted on each contour alone, but only for contours that share no vertex, and only after
Compute() has failed. Fillets that share a vertex were left as they were, which is two defects.

 - Frames and adjacent edges: with radii that cross (a 4 x 10 x 6 box, all four top edges, r = 3)
   or that run out of face (the left top edge r = 4.5 next to the front top edge r = 1) Compute()
   either answers IsDone() == false or answers true with an open shell: an edge that borders one
   face, a volume of 1e26 and more, and a tessellator that never returns.
 - Three edges of one radius at a corner where the fillets meet exactly (r = w/2 on the 4 mm
   width, top and vertical edges): IsDone() == false.

This change widens the fallback and moves its trigger:

 - Two contours may share a vertex where it is a convex corner of three mutually perpendicular
   planar faces whose third edge is not filleted. The two fillets then meet in the intersection of
   their surfaces, which is the intersection of the two single-edge results.
 - Three contours of one radius may meet at such a corner when every edge there is at least 2 r
   long: the result is the intersection of the single-edge results with the corner cube minus the
   ball of radius r (centre r along each edge) cut out, a ball tangent to the three faces and to
   the three cylinders.
 - When Compute() answers done but the result has an edge bordering fewer than two faces and the
   shape did not, and there are several contours, the fallback runs and replaces the result if it
   applies. Where it does not apply the result is left as it was.

Any other vertex (a concave corner, an unequal vertex blend, a vertex blend with a radius past its
face, more than three contours, curved or non-perpendicular faces) is not covered and keeps the
behaviour it had. Every fallback result must still be one valid closed solid that takes material
away and removes at least the maximum and at most the sum (plus the corner pieces) of what the
single contours remove.

Measured (Scripts/repro/fillet-3233/): 31 configurations on 4 x 10 x 6, 10 x 10 x 8 and L and U
extrusions against a reference built from removal prisms and cube-minus-ball pieces with no fillet
code. Frames at r = 2.5, 3, 3.9, 4.5 (and 3 with 1 on the short edges) and 10 x 10 at r = 5 and
6, adjacent edges with one radius past its face, and the r = 2 eight-edge ball case: valid, one
closed solid, volume equal to the reference to 2e-7. 1200 random box cases (two seeds) against
patch 0060: 0 regressed, 0 newly invalid, 290 newly valid, the add-mode ones within grid noise of
an independent prism-union volume. Three of the four new GTests fail on kernel.5 and on kernel.5 plus patches
0059 and 0060, pass with this change; all 16 fillet and 5 chamfer GTests pass.

Tracked as SecondMouseAU/OCCTSwift#3233.

